---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Patio Privacy Planner" description="Plan a patio or balcony with screens on multiple sides, partial walls and railings, and movable furniture.">
<header class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Free planning tool · No account needed</p><h1>Patio Privacy Planner</h1><p class="lead">Measure the floor, describe each side, then arrange furniture directly in your plan.</p></header>
<section class="container section planner-layout">
<form class="panel planner-form" id="privacy-form" novalidate>
<fieldset><legend><span>1</span> Floor &amp; roof</legend>
<div class="field-pair"><div><label for="patio-width">Floor width (ft)</label><input id="patio-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="100" value="10" required/></div><div><label for="depth">Floor depth (ft)</label><input id="depth" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="2" data-max="100" value="8" required/></div></div>
<label for="space">Space type</label><select id="space"><option value="patio">Patio</option><option value="balcony">Balcony</option></select><p class="small">Both use the same floor geometry. Balcony plans include building, guard, and load checks.</p>
<label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="has-roof"/> Roof over the floor</label><div id="roof-fields" hidden><label for="roof-height">Floor to underside of roof (ft)</label><input id="roof-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="2" data-max="30" value="8" disabled required/><p class="small">The drawing uses a flat roof over the full floor.</p></div>
</fieldset>
<fieldset><legend><span>2</span> Sides &amp; privacy screens</legend>
<p class="small">A is far from you in the drawing, C is nearest. B is right, D is left. Select a screen on every side you want to cover.</p>
<div class="boundary-list"><div class="boundary-row" data-side="back" role="group" aria-label="A · far side">
<div class="boundary-options"><strong>A · far side</strong><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="wall" id="back-wall"/>Wall</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="rail" id="back-rail"/>Railing</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="screen" id="back-screen" checked/>Screen</label></div>
<div class="boundary-mixed" hidden><p class="small">Wall and railing share this side. Railing fills the part left over.</p><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="back-wall-length">A · far side: wall length (ft)</label><input id="back-wall-length" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="3" disabled required/></div><div><label for="back-wall-at">Wall position</label><select id="back-wall-at"><option value="start">At start of side</option><option value="end">At end of side</option></select></div></div><p class="small">A and C run left to right; B and D run far to near.</p></div>
<div class="boundary-screen" ><label for="back-screen-width">A · far side: length to cover (ft)</label><input id="back-screen-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="6" placeholder="Blank = entire open or railing portion" /><label for="back-mode">Screen starts</label><select id="back-mode"><option value="full">At the floor, covering the railing too</option><option value="above">Above the railing only</option></select></div>
</div><div class="boundary-row" data-side="right" role="group" aria-label="B · right side">
<div class="boundary-options"><strong>B · right side</strong><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="wall" id="right-wall"/>Wall</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="rail" id="right-rail"/>Railing</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="screen" id="right-screen" />Screen</label></div>
<div class="boundary-mixed" hidden><p class="small">Wall and railing share this side. Railing fills the part left over.</p><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="right-wall-length">B · right side: wall length (ft)</label><input id="right-wall-length" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="3" disabled required/></div><div><label for="right-wall-at">Wall position</label><select id="right-wall-at"><option value="start">At start of side</option><option value="end">At end of side</option></select></div></div><p class="small">A and C run left to right; B and D run far to near.</p></div>
<div class="boundary-screen" hidden><label for="right-screen-width">B · right side: length to cover (ft)</label><input id="right-screen-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="" placeholder="Blank = entire open or railing portion" disabled/><label for="right-mode">Screen starts</label><select id="right-mode"><option value="full">At the floor, covering the railing too</option><option value="above">Above the railing only</option></select></div>
</div><div class="boundary-row" data-side="front" role="group" aria-label="C · near side">
<div class="boundary-options"><strong>C · near side</strong><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="wall" id="front-wall"/>Wall</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="rail" id="front-rail"/>Railing</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="screen" id="front-screen" />Screen</label></div>
<div class="boundary-mixed" hidden><p class="small">Wall and railing share this side. Railing fills the part left over.</p><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="front-wall-length">C · near side: wall length (ft)</label><input id="front-wall-length" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="3" disabled required/></div><div><label for="front-wall-at">Wall position</label><select id="front-wall-at"><option value="start">At start of side</option><option value="end">At end of side</option></select></div></div><p class="small">A and C run left to right; B and D run far to near.</p></div>
<div class="boundary-screen" hidden><label for="front-screen-width">C · near side: length to cover (ft)</label><input id="front-screen-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="" placeholder="Blank = entire open or railing portion" disabled/><label for="front-mode">Screen starts</label><select id="front-mode"><option value="full">At the floor, covering the railing too</option><option value="above">Above the railing only</option></select></div>
</div><div class="boundary-row" data-side="left" role="group" aria-label="D · left side">
<div class="boundary-options"><strong>D · left side</strong><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="wall" id="left-wall"/>Wall</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="rail" id="left-rail"/>Railing</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="screen" id="left-screen" />Screen</label></div>
<div class="boundary-mixed" hidden><p class="small">Wall and railing share this side. Railing fills the part left over.</p><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="left-wall-length">D · left side: wall length (ft)</label><input id="left-wall-length" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="3" disabled required/></div><div><label for="left-wall-at">Wall position</label><select id="left-wall-at"><option value="start">At start of side</option><option value="end">At end of side</option></select></div></div><p class="small">A and C run left to right; B and D run far to near.</p></div>
<div class="boundary-screen" hidden><label for="left-screen-width">D · left side: length to cover (ft)</label><input id="left-screen-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="" placeholder="Blank = entire open or railing portion" disabled/><label for="left-mode">Screen starts</label><select id="left-mode"><option value="full">At the floor, covering the railing too</option><option value="above">Above the railing only</option></select></div>
</div></div>
<div class="field-pair"><div id="wall-fields" hidden><label for="wall-height">Wall height from floor (ft)</label><input id="wall-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="30" value="8" disabled required/></div><div id="rail-fields" hidden><label for="rail-height">Railing height from floor (ft)</label><input id="rail-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="10" value="3.5" disabled required/></div></div>
<div class="field-pair"><div><label for="screen-height">Floor to top of screen (ft)</label><input id="screen-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="10" value="6" required/></div><div><label for="panel-width">Width of one screen module (ft)</label><input id="panel-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="10" value="3" required/></div></div><p class="small">Screen top height is always measured from the floor. Module width means usable coverage of one panel; use product dimensions when known. A point or comma works for decimals.</p>
<details class="cost-details"><summary>Optional: add your own prices</summary><label for="module-price">Price per module (USD)</label><input id="module-price" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0" data-max="100000" placeholder="Leave blank if unknown"/><label for="extra-cost">Additional costs (USD)</label><input id="extra-cost" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0" data-max="100000" value="0"/><p class="small">Assumes the same unit price on all sides. Add supports, delivery, and taxes yourself.</p></details>
</fieldset>
<fieldset><legend><span>3</span> Furniture</legend><label for="furniture">Start with</label><select id="furniture"><option value="none">No furniture</option><option value="bistro">Two chairs and a table</option><option value="bench">Bench and coffee table</option></select>
<div id="furniture-fields" hidden><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="seat-width">Seat / bench width (ft)</label><input id="seat-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="20" value="2" disabled required/></div><div><label for="seat-depth">Seat / bench depth (ft)</label><input id="seat-depth" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="20" value="2" disabled required/></div></div><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="table-width">Table width (ft)</label><input id="table-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="20" value="2" disabled required/></div><div><label for="table-depth">Table depth (ft)</label><input id="table-depth" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="20" value="2" disabled required/></div></div><p class="small">After creating the plan, drag individual pieces on the floor. Or focus a piece and use arrow keys. Heights are illustrative; enter actual floor footprints.</p></div>
</fieldset>
<div class="plan-actions"><button class="button" type="submit">Update my plan →</button><button class="reset-button" type="reset">Start over</button></div><p class="small">Your answers stay on this page. Nothing is sent to us or stored automatically.</p><noscript><p>JavaScript is needed for the planner. Read the <a href="/articles/patio-privacy-ideas-for-renters/">patio privacy guide</a>.</p></noscript>
</form>
<section class="panel planner-result" aria-label="Your patio privacy worksheet"><h2>Your space, your layout</h2><p id="planner-message" class="form-error" role="alert" tabindex="-1" hidden></p><div id="results" role="region" aria-label="Planner results" aria-live="polite" tabindex="-1"><div class="planner-empty"><p class="eyebrow">Example only · 10 × 8 ft floor</p><div id="planner-preview"></div><h3>Build your layout from the floor up.</h3><p>Start with the floor dimensions. Add walls, railings, and screens on sides A–D, then move furniture into place.</p><p class="small">If a combination does not work, this example or your last valid plan stays visible while you correct it.</p></div></div></section>
</section><section class="container planner-guidance"><h2>What the drawing means</h2><p>A rectangular floor, a flat full-area roof, wall/railing sections on four sides, example screen modules, and furniture footprints. Mixed sides use one continuous wall section at the start or end and railing on the rest. Screens start at the beginning of that remaining section.</p><p>The planner checks geometric fit and furniture overlap. It does not assess walking clearance, door swings, wind, structural loads, guard compliance, or mounting methods. Confirm product and building requirements before installation. Read our <a href="/articles/patio-privacy-ideas-for-renters/">patio privacy guide</a>.</p></section>
<script type="module" src="/assets/planner.js?v=editor2-20261014" is:inline></script></Base>
